{"ts": "2026-05-10T00:03:51.902860", "session_id": "demo_session", "user": "Recommend courses for next quarter", "assistant": "Based on your profile (CS sophomore, ICS33 in progress), you should go with **STATS67 + CS122A + ANTHRO2A** for Fall 2025. That’s a solid 12-unit mix that hits major requirements, a GE, and keeps your schedule balanced.\n\n- **STATS67** — required for CS, no prereq issues, and Stern teaches a straightforward stats course. It’s a morning class (9am MWF) but worth locking in early.  \n- **CS122A** — Carey is one of the best-rated CS professors (4.7, 93% would take again). TuTh 11–12:20, no conflicts, and you’ll get a solid intro to databases. Grade distribution is fair (38% A).  \n- **ANTHRO2A** — easy GE-IV with Douglas (4.1 rating, 88% would take again). 45% A rate, MWF 11–11:50 — fits perfectly between STATS67 and CS122A. Zero stress filler.\n\n**Risk warnings:**  \n- STATS67 is at 9am — if you’re not a morning person, that’s the only downside.  \n- ICS46 and CS161 are off the table until you finish ICS33. Don’t try to sneak into ICS46 this fall — you’ll be blocked without the prereq.  \n- No time conflicts among the three above.\n\n**Alternatives if you want more major focus:**  \nSwap ANTHRO2A for **IN4MATX43** (Software Eng with Ziv, MWF 12–12:50, easy grader, 42% A). That gives you three major courses (STATS67, CS122A, IN4MATX43) but it’s a heavier workload — Ziv’s lectures are dry, and STATS67 + CS122A already require decent effort.  \nOr replace ANTHRO2A with **WRITING39C** if you need GE-Ib, but it’s taught by staff (unknown quality) and only 18 seats left — risky.\n\n**Follow-up questions:**  \n- How many units are you aiming for? I can suggest adding a 4th if you want.  \n- Are you avoiding mornings? If so, I can reshuffle.  \n- Want to plan ahead for winter? ICS46 and CS161 will be available after you finish ICS33."}
